{
  // Dependency-vulnerability gate for CI (replaces the bare `npm audit --audit-level=high`,
  // which has no way to record a reasoned exception).
  //
  // The gate stays sharp: anything high/critical that is NOT listed below fails the build.
  // `allowlist` is per-advisory (GHSA id), never per-severity — we do not lower the level.
  //
  // Adding an entry requires, in this file: (1) the advisory id, (2) why it does not apply to
  // THIS codebase, measured — not assumed, (3) an expiry date, (4) what removes the need for it.
  // An expired entry is a task, not a renewal: re-check it, do not extend it by reflex.
  //
  // Policy: docs/development/dependency-audit.md
  "$schema": "https://github.com/IBM/audit-ci/raw/main/docs/schema.json",
  "moderate": false,
  "high": true,
  "critical": true,
  "allowlist": [
    // GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 — react-router "RSC Mode CSRF Bypass Allows Action Execution Before
    // 400 Response" (high). Vulnerable range 7.12.0–8.2.0; there is NO fix in the 7.x line
    // (react-router-dom stops at 7.18.1; the fix is react-router v8 >= 8.2.1, a different
    // package and a breaking upgrade).
    //
    // Why it does not apply to payout (measured 2026-07-29, on this tree):
    //   - The admin console is a **static SPA built by Vite** (`npm run build` = `vite build`,
    //     no SSR entry) and served from `public_html/`. `src/main.tsx` mounts with
    //     `createRoot(...).render(...)`; there is no `hydrateRoot` / `renderToString` /
    //     `renderToPipeableStream` anywhere in `src/` (grep: 0 hits).
    //   - Routing is the **declarative** API — `<BrowserRouter>` + `<Routes>` in `src/App.tsx`
    //     and `src/app/router.tsx`. `createBrowserRouter` / data routers are not used, so there
    //     are no route-level `action:` / `loader:` definitions at all (grep for
    //     `^\s*(action|loader)\s*:` in `src/` matches only audit-log domain fields, never a
    //     route config object).
    //   - No RSC and no server runtime: grep for `react-router/server`, `@react-router/dev`,
    //     `'use server'`, `createStaticHandler`, `createStaticRouter` in `src/` = 0 hits.
    // The advisory's attack path (a server executing a route action before returning 400) has
    // no counterpart in a client-only bundle with no data-router actions.
    //
    // Expiry: 2026-08-31. Removed by the react-router v8 migration wave (bundled with the
    // NENE2 RR8 re-evaluation). If that wave slips past the expiry, the entry must be
    // re-argued in a PR — not silently extended.
    "GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2",

    // GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg — brace-expansion "DoS via unbounded expansion length" (high).
    // Vulnerable range <= 5.0.7; the fix is 5.0.8. We TAKE that fix where it is adoptable —
    // `"brace-expansion@5": "^5.0.8"` in overrides — and this entry covers only what is left.
    //
    // Why the fix is NOT adoptable on the 1.x branch (measured 2026-07-29, #261): there is no
    // patched 1.x release, and forcing 5.0.8 into the 1.x slot with a *flat* override breaks
    // its consumer. brace-expansion 1.x IS the module (`module.exports = expand`); 5.x exports
    // a named `expand`. `minimatch@3.1.5` does `require('brace-expansion')` and calls the
    // module, so the flat override made it throw:
    //     TypeError: expand is not a function   (minimatch.js:271, Minimatch.braceExpand)
    // That is exactly the regression this entry exists to avoid re-introducing. Overriding
    // `minimatch@3` upward instead fails the other way: `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y` does
    // `_interopRequireDefault(require('minimatch'))` and calls the default, which minimatch
    // >= 9 does not provide. Retiring the chain needs an eslint-plugin major upgrade.
    //
    // Why the residual risk is acceptable here (measured 2026-07-29 on this tree):
    //   - **dev-only**: `npm ls brace-expansion --omit=dev --all` is empty. It is in no shipped
    //     bundle and on no request path.
    //   - **exactly one vulnerable copy**: `node_modules/eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y/node_modules/
    //     brace-expansion@1.1.16` (the hoisted copy is 5.0.8). Enumerated with `npm ls
    //     minimatch --all` plus a `find` over node_modules — not assumed from the audit summary.
    //   - The advisory needs an attacker-supplied brace pattern. This copy is reached only by
    //     lint running over our own repo contents, with glob patterns that are literals in
    //     committed config.
    //
    // Expiry: 2026-08-31. Removed by the eslint-plugin major wave that moves jsx-a11y onto
    // `minimatch@10` → `brace-expansion@^5`, or by an upstream 1.x backport. Re-check at
    // expiry — do not extend by reflex. Before ever going back to a flat override, re-run the
    // probe in docs/development/dependency-audit.md.
    "GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg",
  ],
}
